apt 2.7.14 CMake: let FindBerkeley.cmake search the conan package prefix

apt's CMake/FindBerkeley.cmake looks for db.h with find_path(... NO_DEFAULT_PATH)
and a hardcoded list of distro paths (/usr/include/db5, ...).  On a cross
build (OHOS aarch64) the Berkeley DB headers and libdb archive exist only
inside the conan package prefix, which is reachable through the toolchain's
CMAKE_INCLUDE_PATH / CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH but is invisible to find_path when
NO_DEFAULT_PATH is set.  configure then fails with:

  CMake Error: Could not find Berkeley DB >= 4.1 (missing: BERKELEY_INCLUDE_DIRS)
  CMake/FindBerkeley.cmake:57 (find_package_handle_standard_args)
  CMakeLists.txt:95 (find_package)

Fix: drop NO_DEFAULT_PATH.  The explicit distro paths are still searched
first (they win when present, preserving the original BSD db.h avoidance),
and the conan-provided CMAKE_INCLUDE_PATH / CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH act as the
fallback that resolves the cross-compile libdb package.

Verified on the OHOS build: BERKELEY_INCLUDE_DIRS/LIBRARIES now resolve to
the conan libdb package and configure passes.  No effect on distro builds
that have db.h in the explicit paths.

--- a/CMake/FindBerkeley.cmake
+++ b/CMake/FindBerkeley.cmake
@@ -33,8 +33,12 @@
 # THIS SOFTWARE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGE.
 
 
-# We need NO_DEFAULT_PATH here, otherwise CMake helpfully picks up the wrong
-# db.h on BSD systems instead of the Berkeley DB one.
+# The original kept NO_DEFAULT_PATH here so CMake does not pick up the wrong
+# db.h on BSD systems instead of the Berkeley DB one.  The explicit distro
+# paths below are searched first and still win when present; dropping
+# NO_DEFAULT_PATH additionally lets the conan-provided CMAKE_INCLUDE_PATH /
+# CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH (cross-compile package prefix) be searched as a fallback,
+# which is required on OHOS/musl where libdb ships only in the conan package.
 find_path(BERKELEY_INCLUDE_DIRS db.h
   ${CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_INCLUDEDIR}/db5
   /usr/local/include/db5
@@ -47,8 +51,6 @@
   ${CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_INCLUDEDIR}
   /usr/local/include
   /usr/include
-
-  NO_DEFAULT_PATH
 )
 
 find_library(BERKELEY_LIBRARIES NAMES db db-5)
